7","L2-0527","L2-0596","L2-0770","L3-0025","L3-0124","L3-0143","L3-0144","L3-0192","L3-0216","L3-0908","L4-0095","L4-0506","L4-0909","L5-0187","L5-0575","L6-0206","L6-0884","L6-0966","L6-1024","L7-0069","L7-0644","L7-0780","L7-0781","L7-1492","L7-2634","L7-2875","L7-3232","L7-3888","L7-4000","L7-4934","L7-4941","L7-5438"],"chemin":{"hsk":187,"lire":160},"sens":{"statut":"relu","glose":"arriver, atteindre, jusqu'à","acceptions":[]},"exemples":[{"zh":"我到家了。","pinyin":"Wǒ dào jiā le.","fr":"Je suis arrivé chez moi.","statut":"relu"},{"zh":"他从早上工作到晚上。","pinyin":"Tā cóng zǎoshang gōngzuò dào wǎnshang.","fr":"Il travaille du matin au soir.","statut":"relu"}],"origine":{"statut":"relu","etiquette":"atteste","fr":"到 associe 至, arriver, qui porte le sens, et 刂, le couteau, qui donne le son : dāo, proche de dào. Le Shuowen jiezi le définit simplement par arriver, atteindre. Le couteau n'a donc rien à voir avec le sens ; il n'est là que pour la prononciation.","en":"到 pairs 至, to arrive, which carries the meaning, with 刂, knife, which gives the sound: dāo, close to dào. The Shuowen jiezi defines it simply as to arrive, to reach. The knife has nothing to do with the meaning; it is there only for the pronunciation.","roles":{"至":"sens","刂":"son"}}},"悼":{"c":"悼","pinyin":"dào","lectures":["dào"],"niveau":7,"decomposition":{"norme":"GF 0014-2009","parts":["忄","⺊","日","十"],"sources":["cjk-decomp"]},"mots":["L7-0786","L7-5516"],"chemin":{},"sens":{"statut":"relu","glose":"pleurer un mort","acceptions":[{"categorie":"V","fr":"pleurer un mort, être en deuil"}]},"exemples":[],"origine":null},"盗":{"c":"盗","pinyin":"dào","lectures":["dào"],"niveau":6,"decomposition":{"norme":"GF 0014-2009","parts":["冫","欠","皿"],"sources":["cjk-decomp"]},"mots":["L6-0207","L6-0650","L7-0784","L7-0785","L7-1070","L7-1071","L7-1547"],"chemin":{},"sens":{"statut":"relu","glose":"voler, dérober ; voleur","acceptions":[{"categorie":"V","fr":"voler, dérober"},{"categorie":"N","fr":"voleur, brigand"}]},"exemples":[{"zh":"他的银行卡被盗了。","pinyin":"Tā de yínhángkǎ bèi dào le.","fr":"On lui a volé sa carte bancaire.","statut":"relu"}],"origine":null},"稻":{"c":"稻","pinyin":"dào","lectures":["dào"],"niveau":7,"decomposition":{"norme":"GF 0014-2009","parts":["禾","爫","臼"],"sources":["cjk-decomp","surcharge"]},"mots":["L7-0788","L7-3854"],"chemin":{},"sens":{"statut":"relu","glose":"riz, la plante","acceptions":[{"categorie":"N","fr":"riz, la plante"}]},"exemples":[],"origine":null},"道":{"c":"道","pinyin":"dào","lectures":["dào"],"niveau":1,"decomposition":{"norme":"GF 0014-2009","parts":["辶","首"],"sources":["cjk-decomp"]},"mots":["L1-0474","L2-0112","L2-0113","L2-0114","L2-0573","L3-0026","L3-0503","L4-0400","L5-0189","L5-0556","L6-0186","L6-0208","L6-0209","L6-0346","L6-0349","L6-0555","L6-0673","L6-0807","L6-0951","L7-0190","L7-0366","L7-0415","L7-0533","L7-0681","L7-0787","L7-0830","L7-0831","L7-0907","L7-1345","L7-1528","L7-1689","L7-2952","L7-3070","L7-3431","L7-3444","L7-3607","L7-3889","L7-3966","L7-4154","L7-4286"],"chemin":{"hsk":208,"lire":171},"sens":{"statut":"relu","glose":"chemin, voie, dire","acceptions":[]},"exemples":[{"zh":"这道菜是我做的。","pinyin":"Zhè dào cài shì wǒ zuò de.","fr":"C'est moi qui ai préparé ce plat.","statut":"relu"}],"origine":{"statut":"relu","etiquette":"atteste","fr":"Sur les bronzes, 道 montre une tête, 首, au milieu d'un carrefour, 行. Le Shuowen jiezi le glose par « la voie où l'on marche » et l'analyse par 辵, la marche, devenu 辶, et 首. De la route, le sens s'est étendu à la méthode, à la doctrine du Tao, et au verbe « dire ».","en":"On bronzes, 道 shows a head, 首, in the middle of a crossroads, 行. The Shuowen jiezi glosses it as “the way one walks” and analyses it as 辵, walking, now 辶, together with 首. From the road, the meaning widened to a method, to the Taoist Way, and to the verb “to say”.","roles":{"辶":"sens","首":"sens"}}},"得":{"c":"得","pinyin":"dé","lectures":["dé","de","děi"],"niveau":1,"decomposition":{"norme":"GF 0014-2009","parts":["彳","日","一","寸"],"sources":["cjk-decomp","surcharge"]},"mots":["L1-0065","L1-0167","L1-0187","L2-0115","L2-0116","L2-0118","L2-0135","L2-0451","L3-0062","L3-0145","L3-0596","L3-0777","L3-0910","L4-0171","L4-0172","L4-0346","L4-0457","L4-0888","L5-0059","L5-0190","L5-0191","L5-0522","L5-0654","L5-0655","L5-0688","L6-0501","L6-0502","L6-0577","L6-0890","L6-0984","L6-1073","L7-0038","L7-0252","L7-0271","L7-0272","L7-0298","L7-0789","L7-0790","L7-0791","L7-0792","L7-0793","L7-0794","L7-0795","L7-0796","L7-0797","L7-0798","L7-0799","L7-0963","L7-0978","L7-1096","L7-1425","L7-1446","L7-1649","L7-2357","L7-2444","L7-2517","L7-2965","L7-4598","L7-4601","L7-4895"],"chemin":{"hsk":128,"lire":137},"sens":{"statut":"relu","glose":"obtenir, gagner, marque de complément","acceptions":[]},"exemples":[{"zh":"他跑得很快。","pinyin":"Tā pǎo de hěn kuài.","fr":"Il court très vite.","statut":"relu"},{"zh":"我得走了。","pinyin":"Wǒ děi zǒu le.","fr":"Je dois y aller.","statut":"relu"}],"origine":{"statut":"relu","etiquette":"atteste","fr":"Sur les os oraculaires, 得 montre une main qui saisit un coquillage 贝, la monnaie de l'époque, parfois au bord d'un chemin 彳. Le Shuowen jiezi le glose par « obtenir en marchant », ce qu'on trouve en route. Dans l'écriture actuelle, le coquillage s'est réduit à 日 sur un trait 一, et la main est devenue 寸.","en":"On oracle bones, 得 shows a hand grasping a cowrie shell 贝, the money of the time, sometimes beside a road 彳. The Shuowen jiezi glosses it as getting something while on the move, what one finds along the way. In today's script the shell has shrunk to 日 over a stroke 一, and the hand has become 寸.","roles":{"彳":"sens","日":"forme","一":"forme","寸":"sens"}}},"德":{"c":"德","pinyin":"dé","lectures":["dé"],"niveau":5,"decomposition":{"norme":"GF 0014-2009","parts":["彳","十","罒","一","心"],"sources":["cjk-decomp","surcharge"]},"mots":["L5-0189","L7-0800","L7-2820","L7-3131"],"chemin":{},"sens":{"statut":"relu","glose":"vertu, morale ; bienfait","acceptions":[{"categorie":"N","fr":"vertu, morale, qualités morales"},{"categorie":"N","fr":"Allemagne, dans Déguó"}]},"exemples":[{"zh":"他在德国学习。","pinyin":"Tā zài Déguó xuéxí.","fr":"Il fait ses études en Allemagne.","statut":"relu"}],"origine":null},"的":{"c":"的","pinyin":"de","lectures":["de","dì","dí","dī"],"niveau":1,"decomposition":{"norme":"GF 0014-2009","parts":["白","勺"],"sources":["cjk-decomp"]},"mots":["L1-0026","L1-0067","L1-0442","L1-0471","L2-0117","L2-0384","L3-0862","L4-0178","L4-0647","L7-2807","L7-2938","L7-3896","L7-5071","L7-5300","L7-5583"],"chemin":{"hsk":197,"lire":166},"sens":{"statut":"relu","glose":"marque de détermination","acceptions":[]},"exemples":[{"zh":"这是我的书。","pinyin":"Zhè shì wǒ de shū.","fr":"C'est mon livre.","statut":"relu"},{"zh":"他是开车的。","pinyin":"Tā shì kāichē de.","fr":"Il est chauffeur.","statut":"relu"}],"origine":{"statut":"relu","etiquette":"atteste","fr":"Le Shuowen jiezi enregistre ce caractère sous la forme 旳, « clair, brillant », avec 日 pour le sens et 勺 pour le son ; 白, clair lui aussi, a pris ensuite la place de 日. De la tache claire, le sens est passé au centre de la cible, qu'on retrouve dans 目的, « le but ». La particule de, le mot le plus fréquent du chinois, est un emprunt : elle a pris ce caractère pour sa seule prononciation, et 勺, lu sháo, n'en donne plus le son.","en":"The Shuowen jiezi records this character as 旳, “bright, clear”, with 日 for the meaning and 勺 for the sound; 白, also bright, later took the place of 日. From a bright spot, the meaning moved to the centre of a target, still found in 目的, “goal”. The particle de, the most frequent word in Chinese, is a loan: it took this character for its sound alone, and 勺, read sháo, no longer gives that sound.","roles":{"白":"sens","勺":"forme"}}},"灯":{"c":"灯","pinyin":"dēng","lectures":["dēng"],"niveau":2,"decomposition":{"norme":"GF 0014-2009","parts":["火","丁"],"sources":["cjk-decomp"]},"mots":["L2-0119","L4-0173","L4-0188","L6-0782","L7-0801","L7-0802","L7-1662","L7-2718","L7-2734","L7-5248"],"c